  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single storey rear extension, by reason of its excessive depth, height and position adjacent to the boundary with 251a Jersey Road, would be an intrusive and unneighbourly addition, as well as having a serious and adverse effect on the amenities enjoyed by occupants of neighbouring property causing loss of light and outlook, contrary to Local Plan Policies SC7, CC1 and CC2, and Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed single storey rear extension and front gate by virtue of their design and appearance would represent an incongruous addition which would harm the character and appearance of the host property and Osterley Park Conservation Area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policies Local Plan Policies CC1, CC2, CC4 and SC7 and Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal fails to demonstrate that the required visibility splays would be achieved and that vehicles can enter and exit the site in a safe manner. The proposal would fail to provide a separate 1.2m wide pedestrian path from the footway to the dwelling's front door. The application would therefore fail to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in harm to highway and pedestrian safety, contrary to Local Plan policy EC2 and the Council's Residential Crossover and Off- Street Parking Policy SPD."
  ],
  "decision": "Refused",
  "appeal_decision": null,
